.TH "webveld\-validate" "1" "2026\-11\-02" "WebVeld 0.10.1" "User Commands"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
webveld\-validate \- reference conformance validator for the WebVeld specification
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBwebveld\-validate\fR [\fB\-\-classify\fR] [\fB\-\-css\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR=\fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR] \fIFILE\fR.\&.\&.\&
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBwebveld\-validate\fR checks HTML documents and style sheets against the
normative WebVeld specification.\& WebVeld is a family of minimal subsets of
HTML5 and CSS for documents that look the same in a purpose\-built minimalist
browser and in any modern web browser.\&
.PP
The element, attribute, CSS property, and input\-type allowlists are read from
the specification'\&s own tables at run time, so they cannot drift from the
specification.\& Enumerated values, selectors, and units are checked against
the specification by the test suite.\&
.PP
Spec section 2.\&6 defines conformance as two passes:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP 1. 4
\fBHTML5 validity\fR, checked by a standard validator such as the Nu Html
Checker (spec section 2.\&3 item 1).\&
.IP 2. 4
\fBSubset conformance\fR against spec sections 4 to 9, which this tool checks.\&
.PD
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-\-classify\fR
.RS 4
Report each document as one of the three states of spec section 2.\&6:
.PP
\fBConforming\fR: the document satisfies spec section 2.\&3.\&
.PP
\fBExtended\fR: the document has scripting, a \fBnoscript\fR element whose
content conforms, and is otherwise conforming (spec section 2.\&5).\& This is not an
error.\&
.PP
\fBNon\-conforming\fR: everything else.\&
.PP
In this mode the exit status is non\-zero only if a file is
Non\-conforming.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-css\fR
.RS 4
Treat every input as a style sheet rather than a document.\& Files ending
in \fI.\&css\fR are detected without this.\& The style sheet is wrapped in a
minimal conforming document, so every finding is the style sheet'\&s own.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-format\fR=\fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR
.RS 4
Output format.\& \fBjson\fR emits one record per input with its path, kind,
state, and findings.\& The banner showing the allowlist sizes is omitted in
this mode.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH CHECKS
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
Elements (spec section 4.\&3), attributes (spec sections 5.\&1 to 5.\&2), and enumerated
attribute values: \fBtabindex\fR, \fBdir\fR, \fBmeta\fR names and \fBog:*\fR properties,
\fBlink rel\fR, and \fBchecked\fR only on checkboxes and radio buttons.\&
.IP \(bu 4
Document structure: doctype, \fBlang\fR, UTF\-8 charset, one \fBtitle\fR, at most
one \fBmain\fR, and \fBdetails\fR starting with \fBsummary\fR (spec sections 4.\&1 to 4.\&3).\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBnoscript\fR only in extended documents (spec section 2.\&3 item 7).\&
.IP \(bu 4
No inline \fBstyle\fR attributes and no author \fB!\&important\fR (spec section 6.\&1).\&
.IP \(bu 4
CSS properties and values, including the CSS\-wide keywords (spec section 6.\&2);
selectors (spec section 6.\&3); units (spec section 6.\&4); and the bounded grid subset.\&
.IP \(bu 4
Media queries: permitted features and \fBprefers\-color\-scheme\fR values,
only the \fBprint\fR media type, no \fBnot\fR or \fBonly\fR, no range syntax, no
nesting, and no \fBurl()\fR inside a query (spec section 6.\&6).\&
.IP \(bu 4
Fonts: no \fBlocal()\fR and no cross\-origin \fBsrc\fR (spec section 6.\&5).\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fB:visited\fR limited to color properties (spec section 6.\&3).\&
.IP \(bu 4
URLs by position: same\-origin subresources, \fBdata:\fR only for PNG and JPEG
images and PNG icons, and no \fBjavascript:\fR, \fBvbscript:\fR, \fBdata:\fR, or
\fBfile:\fR links (spec sections 7.\&1 to 7.\&2).\&
.IP \(bu 4
Images are PNG or JPEG, and site icons are PNG (spec section 7.\&4).\&
.IP \(bu 4
Forms: HTTP or HTTPS \fBaction\fR, GET or POST \fBmethod\fR, permitted input
types, safe \fBpattern\fR expressions, HTTPS for password forms, and permitted
\fBautocomplete\fR tokens (spec section 5.\&2).\&
.IP \(bu 4
Viewport declarations that disable zoom (spec section 5.\&2).\&
.IP \(bu 4
Accessibility: \fBalt\fR on images, label counts, heading order, and focus
outlines that are not removed without a replacement (spec section 9).\&
.PD
.PP
A clean report means nothing detectable is wrong.\& The tool reads source
text with patterns rather than building a full HTML tree, so run an HTML5
validator as well.\&
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Every file conforms (with \fB\-\-classify\fR: every file is Conforming or
Extended).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
At least one file does not conform (with \fB\-\-classify\fR: is
Non\-conforming), or an error occurred.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBWEBVELD_SPEC\fR
.RS 4
Path to the WebVeld specification (\fIwebveld\-spec.\&md\fR).\& If unset, the
validator looks in the current directory, next to its install location,
and in the standard data directories such as
\fI/usr/local/share/webveld/doc/webveld\-spec.\&md\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Validate a document:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
webveld\-validate index\&.html
.fi
.RE
.PP
Classify several documents:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
webveld\-validate \-\-classify site/*\&.html
.fi
.RE
.PP
Validate against a specific copy of the specification:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
WEBVELD_SPEC=/opt/webveld/webveld\-spec\&.md webveld\-validate page\&.html
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBwebveld\-profile\-check\fR(1), \fBwebveld\fR(7)
